==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*5 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*4 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*2 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*1 [[Selena]] spawns as the boss after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*1 [[Bearkini]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] for the Heavenly Hippoes and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]], and other long-ranged units for the Bearkinis and Selena. The Trolly Bloggers can be a bit of an issue, but as long as you have enough spammable [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|area attackers]] for them, they should not pose a threat to Artist Cat and your other [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]].

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Never Not Summer! (Monthly Event)|Never Not Summer!]] stages, Heat Wave Blues' Japanese name, Summertime Blues Three, is a reference to a song, in this case "[https://youtu.be/L97GrvDPocc Summertime Blues]" by [[wikipedia:Misato Watanabe|Misato Watanabe]].
**Interestingly, サマータイムブルースリー can be read as either "Summertime Blues Three" or "Summertime [[wikipedia:Bruce Lee|Bruce Lee]]".

